Yes, and it's a pitty that you just lose the scroll instead of being
told that it's too far and are allowed to retry. Here's some data to
consider before applying the scroll... (as far as I read the code
correctly)

Maximum distance to place the target is:  dx^2 + dy^2 < 32
(E.g. that is a distance of 5 squares in a straight orthogonal line,
diagonally it's just 3 squares); otherwise you will just smell the
rotten eggs.

The effective cloud radius and damage depends on the BUC status of the
scroll:
                  radius   damage
    cursed          2         4
    uncursed        3         8
    blessed         4        16

The duration of the cloud effect is 4..6 turns.

